    {
      "id": "c13-l3",
      "title": "swap",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The classic example from Kernighan and Ritchie's book: a function that swaps two variables. With plain int parameters it can't work, because it would only swap its copies.",
        "With pointers, it works: void swap(int *a, int *b) { int t = *a; *a = *b; *b = t; }, called as swap(&x, &y);.",
        "Pointers can also point to nothing: 0, written NULL. Checking if (p != NULL) before following a pointer avoids many crashes."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "void swap(int *a, int *b) {",
          "    int t = *a;",
          "    *a = *b;",
          "    *b = t;",
          "}",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int x = 1, y = 2;",
          "    swap(&x, &y);",
          "    printf(\"x = %d, y = %d\\n\", x, y);",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "x = 2, y = 1"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c13-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why can't void swap(int a, int b) swap the caller's variables?",
          "options": [
            "It only gets copies",
            "int can't be swapped",
            "It needs a return value",
            "It can"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Call by value: the copies are swapped, and then thrown away."
        },
        {
          "id": "c13-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How is the pointer version of swap called?",
          "options": [
            "swap(&x, &y);",
            "swap(x, y);",
            "swap(*x, *y);",
            "x = swap(y);"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Pass the addresses."
        },
        {
          "id": "c13-l3-e3",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the body of swap in the right order.",
          "lines": [
            "void swap(int *a, int *b) {",
            "    int t = *a;",
            "    *a = *b;",
            "    *b = t;",
            "}"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "void swap(int *a, int *b) {",
            "    int t = *a;",
            "    *a = *b;",
            "    *b = t;",
            "}"
          ],
          "explanation": "Save *a first, then overwrite it, then use the saved value."
        },
